  "narrative": {
    "intro": "National Steel and Shipbuilding obligated $2.8B in federal contract obligations in FY2026 to date. National Steel and Shipbuilding received 16 awards so far in the fiscal year, with an average award size of $173M. National Steel and Shipbuilding’s current-year obligations are up 403.7% year over year, reflecting a large increase compared with the prior fiscal year total. Historical obligations show that National Steel and Shipbuilding had $471M in FY21, $2.2B in FY22, $1.2B in FY23, $1.4B in FY24, and $550M in FY25. National Steel and Shipbuilding’s FY2026 total is a partial, fiscal-year-to-date figure and should be read as such relative to full-year totals. This snapshot highlights that National Steel and Shipbuilding’s federal receipts have moved substantially across recent years, with FY22 and FY26 standing out as the largest obligation years in the series.",
